title the copy GitHub keeps -- the badge popover names the gap, and one re-upload cures both Codex clones
prompt Keaton verified the kaexvx9 address on his account yet the badges held; the popover on the nine-seats commit read that the email in the signature does not match the committer email, key 635BDFCEB8C4309E.
think The mechanism, made plain: GitHub compares a commit's committer email against the UID emails inside ITS OWN STORED COPY of the signing key, and that copy still carries only the elder kaexvx9 UID -- the keaton.dunsford UID added last night lives in the local Homebrew keyring until the key is re-uploaded. So the account-side email verify was the necessary half (stored UIDs must be verified addresses) and the key re-upload is the sufficient half. The screenshot also settles a wider fact: Mystery's map commit wears the same badge, so BOTH Codex clones sign with the one host trio key, and the single delete-and-re-add at Keaton's keys cures grain-mind and grain-mystery history together, retroactively, with no clone or commit touched.
obs Counsel only; the two gh lines ride in the reply. The fleet's day continues on the remotes meanwhile.
loom key_short=635BDFCEB8C4309E stored_uids=kaexvx9_only cure=delete_and_readd clones_covered=2
